# size 20x5
# What an erase leaves behind, style-wise.
#
# Erasing fills with the current BACKGROUND and nothing else. Not the whole active style: an
# underline on a blank cell is visible - it draws as a line - so an emulator that carries the full
# style into erased cells paints underscores across a row that a real terminal leaves empty.
#
# Row 1: underlined red text, then erase to end of line. The tail must be plain.
# Row 3: text on a blue background, then erase to end of line. The tail keeps the background,
#        because that part IS what a terminal carries.
\e[H\e[4;31mUNDER\e[K
\e[3;1H\e[0m\e[44mBLUE\e[K
\e[5;1H\e[0mdone
